---

<Base
  title="Stuart Lee"
  description="Stuart Lee — data scientist working in genomics."
>
  <header class="intro">
    <Image
      src={headshot}
      alt="Photo of Stuart Lee"
      width={220}
      densities={[1, 2]}
      class="headshot"
    />
    <div>
      <h1>Stuart Lee</h1>
      <div class="links">
        <a href="mailto:stuart.andrew.lee@gmail.com">Contact me</a>
        <a href="https://meet.stuartlee.org">Book a call</a>
        {
          iconLinks.map((link) => (
            <a
              href={link.href}
              aria-label={link.label}
              title={link.label}
              class="icon"
            >
              <svg
                viewBox={link.viewBox}
                width="20"
                height="20"
                fill="currentColor"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d={link.path} />
              </svg>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <p>I'm Stuart, a data scientist who works in genomics.</p>

  <p>
    At <a href="https://www.wehi.edu.au/">WEHI</a> I research how short tandem repeats
    drive neurodegenerative diseases, using large cohorts like UK Biobank and Genomics
    England. I'm also interested in how we interpret prediction models—particularly
    as genetic risk scores and biological foundation models become widespread. Previously
    I built analytics tools at Genentech and research applications at the University
    of Melbourne.
  </p>

  <p>
    I created <a href="https://tidyomics.github.io/plyranges/">plyranges</a>,
    which brings tidy data principles to genomics and is now part of the
    <a href="https://tidyomics.github.io/tidyomics/">tidyomics</a> ecosystem.
  </p>

  <p>
    In my PhD days I wrote some
    <a href="https://archive.stuartlee.org">blogs</a> about teaching data
    science.
  </p>

  <p>
    I care about making data science accessible to people without quantitative
    backgrounds, which shapes how I build software and teach.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .intro h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .headshot {
    width: 110px;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .links {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .links a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .links a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .links a.icon {
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 0.15rem;
  }

  .links svg {
    display: block;
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .intro {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }
</style>
